APPROVED
By Stefanle Boster at 10:53am, Oct05,2022
MEMORANDUM OF UNDERSTANDING
BETWEEN LARAMIE COUNTY COMMUNITY COLLEGE AND
THE CITY OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING
1
Parties.This Memorandum of Understanding(MOU) is made and entered into by and
between Laramie County Community College(LCCC), whose addressis 1400 ECollege
Drive, Cheyenne, WY 82007, and the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming,(City)whose
addressis2101O'Neil Avenue, Cheyenne, Wyoming82001.
2.
Purpose.To set out the responsibilities for LCCC's CDL“Your Truck”Training
Program to utilize the City's truck/trailer while receiving instructions from a LCCC
trainer using the City'slocation as the base for this training.
LCCC will provide a CDL instructor exclusively to the City in order to provide the
following training:
·Theory training (online)(30days to complete 17-20hours of online
training -from home, place of work, etc.)
Simulator training for shifting, turning, driving, and backing (up to 8
hours -provided on LCCC campus)
·Lecture training (in person) (lectures vary in length, 1-3 hours -provided
on LCC C campus)
·Behind thewheel training (BTW)(in person)
oBTW training can be adjusted based on trainee's previous
experience and capabilities
o Class A CDL training-Not to exceed 60 hours of BTW training
0Class B, C, and Hotshot training-Not toexceed 50 hours of BTW
training
BTW training does not include all additional training hours that the
trainee receives.Only BTWhours are logged into the Training Provider
Register (TPR) at the conclusion of training.
Trainee to instructor ratio is2:1(maximum)
The programwill utilize the City's trucks and trailers toperform the BTW training.The
BTWtraining will occur on rural, suburban, city, state highways, and UShighways
the CDL curriculum.The radius of training shall be limited100 miles and is limited to
the State of Wyoming.Inaddition, the truck/trailer will beused to demonstrate an
inspection at a Port of Entryduring the BTW training.The City shallensure that the
vehicle will be registered with the proper authorities.
3.
TermofMOU.ThisMOU shall commence upon date of last signature and shallremain
in full force and, thereafter, shall automatically renew, unless otherwise terminated.
Memorandum of Understanding“Your Truck” Training Program
